1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,833
One prophet is named

2
00:00:01,853 --> 00:00:02,983
in the Quran

3
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:04,840
more than any other.

4
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:06,465
Not once or twice,

5
00:00:06,485 --> 00:00:07,754
but one hundred

6
00:00:07,774 --> 00:00:09,287
and thirty-six times,

7
00:00:09,307 --> 00:00:11,189
across thirty-four surahs.

8
00:00:11,209 --> 00:00:12,768
His name is Musa,

9
00:00:12,788 --> 00:00:14,533
peace be upon him.

10
00:00:14,553 --> 00:00:16,158
This is his story,

11
00:00:16,178 --> 00:00:17,308
told the way

12
00:00:17,328 --> 00:00:19,219
the Quran tells it.

13
00:00:19,239 --> 00:00:20,292
Surah Al-Qasas,

14
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:21,272
the Stories,

15
00:00:21,292 --> 00:00:24,003
opens his story with a promise.

16
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:25,798
Allah recites the news

17
00:00:25,818 --> 00:00:28,298
of Musa and Pharaoh in truth,

18
00:00:28,318 --> 00:00:30,393
for people who believe.

19
00:00:30,413 --> 00:00:32,063
It begins in Egypt,

20
00:00:32,083 --> 00:00:34,519
on the banks of the Nile.

21
00:00:34,539 --> 00:00:36,405
Pharaoh had made himself

22
00:00:36,425 --> 00:00:38,170
great in the land.

23
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:40,808
He split its people into groups,

24
00:00:40,828 --> 00:00:42,064
and one group,

25
00:00:42,084 --> 00:00:43,919
the Children of Israel,

26
00:00:43,939 --> 00:00:44,994
he crushed.

27
00:00:45,014 --> 00:00:47,541
Their newborn sons were killed.

28
00:00:47,561 --> 00:00:50,234
Their daughters were left alive.

29
00:00:50,254 --> 00:00:51,845
But the Quran says

30
00:00:51,865 --> 00:00:54,070
Allah wanted something else.

31
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:55,727
He wanted to favour

32
00:00:55,747 --> 00:00:58,088
the people who were oppressed,

33
00:00:58,108 --> 00:00:59,192
and to make

34
00:00:59,212 --> 00:01:01,518
them leaders and inheritors.

35
00:01:01,538 --> 00:01:02,820
Into this fear,

36
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:04,861
a baby boy was born.

37
00:01:04,881 --> 00:01:06,150
His mother knew

38
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:08,881
what happened to boys like him.

39
00:01:08,901 --> 00:01:10,354
Then Allah inspired

40
00:01:10,374 --> 00:01:12,195
her with an instruction

41
00:01:12,215 --> 00:01:14,106
that sounds impossible.

42
00:01:14,126 --> 00:01:14,994
Nurse him,

43
00:01:15,014 --> 00:01:17,355
and when you fear for him,

44
00:01:17,375 --> 00:01:19,580
cast him into the river.

45
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:20,685
Do not fear

46
00:01:20,705 --> 00:01:22,450
and do not grieve.

47
00:01:22,470 --> 00:01:24,811
We will return him to you,

48
00:01:24,831 --> 00:01:25,961
and make him

49
00:01:25,981 --> 00:01:28,010
one of the messengers.

50
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:29,943
So she placed her son

51
00:01:29,963 --> 00:01:31,002
in a chest

52
00:01:31,022 --> 00:01:33,503
and let the river take it.

53
00:01:33,523 --> 00:01:35,252
The water carried him

54
00:01:35,272 --> 00:01:36,508
away from her,

55
00:01:36,528 --> 00:01:37,259
downstream,

56
00:01:37,279 --> 00:01:38,639
toward the palace

57
00:01:38,659 --> 00:01:40,112
of the very man

58
00:01:40,132 --> 00:01:42,898
who was killing boys like him.

59
00:01:42,918 --> 00:01:44,370
The Quran describes

60
00:01:44,390 --> 00:01:46,363
her heart in one word:

61
00:01:46,383 --> 00:01:47,023
empty.

62
00:01:47,043 --> 00:01:49,661
She almost gave the secret away,

63
00:01:49,681 --> 00:01:52,346
but Allah held her heart firm.

64
00:01:52,366 --> 00:01:54,385
She said to his sister,

65
00:01:54,405 --> 00:01:55,560
follow him.

66
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:56,802
The chest came

67
00:01:56,822 --> 00:01:59,163
to the bank by the palace,

68
00:01:59,183 --> 00:02:01,142
and Pharaoh's family lifted

69
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:03,644
the baby out of the water.

70
00:02:03,664 --> 00:02:05,130
Pharaoh's wife said:

71
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:07,077
a comfort of the eye,

72
00:02:07,097 --> 00:02:09,072
for me and for you.

73
00:02:09,092 --> 00:02:10,745
Do not kill him.

74
00:02:10,765 --> 00:02:12,968
Perhaps he will benefit us,

75
00:02:12,988 --> 00:02:14,487
or we will adopt

76
00:02:14,507 --> 00:02:16,121
him as a son.

77
00:02:16,141 --> 00:02:18,715
But the baby would not feed.

78
00:02:18,735 --> 00:02:19,957
Allah had kept

79
00:02:19,977 --> 00:02:22,228
every wet nurse from him.

80
00:02:22,248 --> 00:02:23,163
His sister,

81
00:02:23,183 --> 00:02:25,110
watching from a distance,

82
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:26,414
stepped forward.

83
00:02:26,434 --> 00:02:27,565
Shall I show

84
00:02:27,585 --> 00:02:28,854
you a household

85
00:02:28,874 --> 00:02:31,133
that will care for him?

86
00:02:31,153 --> 00:02:32,237
And so Musa

87
00:02:32,257 --> 00:02:34,969
was returned to his own mother.

88
00:02:34,989 --> 00:02:36,211
The Quran says

89
00:02:36,231 --> 00:02:36,901
it was

90
00:02:36,921 --> 00:02:39,401
so that she would be content,

91
00:02:39,421 --> 00:02:40,703
and not grieve,

92
00:02:40,723 --> 00:02:41,486
and know

93
00:02:41,506 --> 00:02:42,820
that the promise

94
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:44,639
of Allah is true.

95
00:02:44,659 --> 00:02:47,371
Musa grew up in Pharaoh's house.

96
00:02:47,391 --> 00:02:48,659
When he reached

97
00:02:48,679 --> 00:02:50,100
his full strength,

98
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,343
Allah gave him

99
00:02:51,363 --> 00:02:53,299
judgement and knowledge.

100
00:02:53,319 --> 00:02:54,910
One day he entered

101
00:02:54,930 --> 00:02:57,165
the city at a quiet hour

102
00:02:57,185 --> 00:02:59,388
and found two men fighting,

103
00:02:59,408 --> 00:03:01,473
one from his own people,

104
00:03:01,493 --> 00:03:03,054
one from Pharaoh's.

105
00:03:03,074 --> 00:03:05,079
The man from his people

106
00:03:05,099 --> 00:03:07,258
called to him for help.

107
00:03:07,278 --> 00:03:09,435
Musa struck the other man,

108
00:03:09,455 --> 00:03:11,660
and the blow killed him.

109
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:14,216
He had not meant to kill.

110
00:03:14,236 --> 00:03:15,734
Musa turned straight

111
00:03:15,754 --> 00:03:17,039
to his Lord.

112
00:03:17,059 --> 00:03:17,835
My Lord,

113
00:03:17,855 --> 00:03:19,644
I have wronged myself,

114
00:03:19,664 --> 00:03:21,041
so forgive me.

115
00:03:21,061 --> 00:03:22,990
And Allah forgave him.

116
00:03:23,010 --> 00:03:24,706
He is the Forgiving,

117
00:03:24,726 --> 00:03:25,973
the Merciful.

118
00:03:25,993 --> 00:03:27,768
The next day a man

119
00:03:27,788 --> 00:03:28,734
came running

120
00:03:28,754 --> 00:03:31,558
from the far end of the city.

121
00:03:31,578 --> 00:03:33,445
The leaders are plotting

122
00:03:33,465 --> 00:03:34,609
to kill you,

123
00:03:34,629 --> 00:03:35,546
he said.

124
00:03:35,566 --> 00:03:36,306
Leave.

125
00:03:36,326 --> 00:03:37,917
So Musa left Egypt

126
00:03:37,937 --> 00:03:39,451
alone and afraid.

127
00:03:39,471 --> 00:03:41,154
He walked out across

128
00:03:41,174 --> 00:03:43,101
the desert toward Madyan,

129
00:03:43,121 --> 00:03:43,667
saying,

130
00:03:43,687 --> 00:03:45,831
perhaps my Lord will guide

131
00:03:45,851 --> 00:03:47,972
me to the right way.

132
00:03:47,992 --> 00:03:49,965
At the well of Madyan,

133
00:03:49,985 --> 00:03:51,161
shepherds crowded

134
00:03:51,181 --> 00:03:52,696
around the water.

135
00:03:52,716 --> 00:03:54,229
Off to one side,

136
00:03:54,249 --> 00:03:57,006
two women held their flock back.

137
00:03:57,026 --> 00:03:58,755
We cannot water until

138
00:03:58,775 --> 00:04:00,288
the shepherds leave,

139
00:04:00,308 --> 00:04:01,176
they said,

140
00:04:01,196 --> 00:04:02,419
and our father

141
00:04:02,439 --> 00:04:04,099
is an old man.

142
00:04:04,119 --> 00:04:05,066
Musa watered

143
00:04:05,086 --> 00:04:06,969
their flock for them.

144
00:04:06,989 --> 00:04:08,533
Then he went back

145
00:04:08,553 --> 00:04:09,776
into the shade

146
00:04:09,796 --> 00:04:12,101
and made a short prayer.

147
00:04:12,121 --> 00:04:12,898
My Lord,

148
00:04:12,918 --> 00:04:14,232
I am in need

149
00:04:14,252 --> 00:04:15,567
of whatever good

150
00:04:15,587 --> 00:04:17,608
You send down to me.

151
00:04:17,628 --> 00:04:18,542
A stranger,

152
00:04:18,562 --> 00:04:19,891
tired and alone,

153
00:04:19,911 --> 00:04:21,894
asking only for good.

154
00:04:21,914 --> 00:04:23,735
The answer came walking

155
00:04:23,755 --> 00:04:25,776
toward him with shyness.

156
00:04:25,796 --> 00:04:27,769
One of the women said,

157
00:04:27,789 --> 00:04:29,578
my father invites you,

158
00:04:29,598 --> 00:04:30,406
to reward

159
00:04:30,426 --> 00:04:32,769
you for watering our flock.

160
00:04:32,789 --> 00:04:34,104
Her father heard

161
00:04:34,124 --> 00:04:36,143
his story and told him:

162
00:04:36,163 --> 00:04:37,125
fear not.

163
00:04:37,145 --> 00:04:38,460
You have escaped

164
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:40,325
the wrongdoing people.

165
00:04:40,345 --> 00:04:42,028
One of the daughters

166
00:04:42,048 --> 00:04:43,068
said, father,

167
00:04:43,088 --> 00:04:44,050
hire him.

168
00:04:44,070 --> 00:04:44,833
The best

169
00:04:44,853 --> 00:04:45,937
one to hire

170
00:04:45,957 --> 00:04:47,134
is the strong

171
00:04:47,154 --> 00:04:48,807
and the trustworthy.

172
00:04:48,827 --> 00:04:51,246
Her father offered Musa marriage

173
00:04:51,266 --> 00:04:53,331
to one of his daughters,

174
00:04:53,351 --> 00:04:55,416
for eight years of work,

175
00:04:55,436 --> 00:04:57,411
or ten if he chose.

176
00:04:57,431 --> 00:04:58,391
Musa stayed,

177
00:04:58,411 --> 00:05:00,486
and completed the term.

178
00:05:00,506 --> 00:05:01,467
Years later,

179
00:05:01,487 --> 00:05:02,940
Musa was travelling

180
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:04,781
with his family through

181
00:05:04,801 --> 00:05:06,269
the dark desert.

182
00:05:06,289 --> 00:05:08,722
On the side of the mountain,

183
00:05:08,742 --> 00:05:10,303
he saw a fire.

184
00:05:10,323 --> 00:05:11,192
Stay here,

185
00:05:11,212 --> 00:05:12,542
he told them.

186
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:14,199
Perhaps I can bring

187
00:05:14,219 --> 00:05:15,364
you a torch,

188
00:05:15,384 --> 00:05:17,112
or find some guidance

189
00:05:17,132 --> 00:05:18,517
at the fire.

190
00:05:18,537 --> 00:05:20,372
When he came to it,

191
00:05:20,392 --> 00:05:21,569
he was called

192
00:05:21,589 --> 00:05:22,811
from the right

193
00:05:22,831 --> 00:05:24,482
side of the valley,

194
00:05:24,502 --> 00:05:25,647
from a tree,

195
00:05:25,667 --> 00:05:27,411
in a blessed spot.

196
00:05:27,431 --> 00:05:28,402
O Musa.

197
00:05:28,422 --> 00:05:30,455
Indeed, I am your Lord,

198
00:05:30,475 --> 00:05:32,450
so remove your sandals.

199
00:05:32,470 --> 00:05:33,186
You are

200
00:05:33,206 --> 00:05:35,925
in the sacred valley of Tuwa.

201
00:05:35,945 --> 00:05:37,550
I have chosen you,

202
00:05:37,570 --> 00:05:40,235
so listen to what is revealed.

203
00:05:40,255 --> 00:05:41,354
I am Allah,

204
00:05:41,374 --> 00:05:43,577
there is no god but Me,

205
00:05:43,597 --> 00:05:44,834
so worship Me,

206
00:05:44,854 --> 00:05:46,352
and establish prayer

207
00:05:46,372 --> 00:05:48,079
for My remembrance.

208
00:05:48,099 --> 00:05:49,568
Then a question.

209
00:05:49,588 --> 00:05:50,304
What is

210
00:05:50,324 --> 00:05:52,389
that in your right hand,

211
00:05:52,409 --> 00:05:53,280
O Musa?

212
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,766
It is my staff,

213
00:05:54,786 --> 00:05:55,703
he said.

214
00:05:55,723 --> 00:05:57,097
I lean on it,

215
00:05:57,117 --> 00:05:58,754
I bring down leaves

216
00:05:58,774 --> 00:05:59,965
for my sheep,

217
00:05:59,985 --> 00:06:01,484
and I have other

218
00:06:01,504 --> 00:06:02,788
uses for it.

219
00:06:02,808 --> 00:06:04,045
Throw it down,

220
00:06:04,065 --> 00:06:05,449
he was told.

221
00:06:05,469 --> 00:06:06,614
He threw it,

222
00:06:06,634 --> 00:06:08,607
and it became a snake,

223
00:06:08,627 --> 00:06:09,727
moving fast.

224
00:06:09,747 --> 00:06:11,584
Musa turned and ran.

225
00:06:11,604 --> 00:06:13,945
Come back and do not fear,

226
00:06:13,965 --> 00:06:15,250
he was told.

227
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:16,232
Seize it.

228
00:06:16,252 --> 00:06:17,475
We will return

229
00:06:17,495 --> 00:06:19,524
it to what it was.

230
00:06:19,544 --> 00:06:21,335
Then a second sign.

231
00:06:21,355 --> 00:06:23,972
Put your hand into your garment,

232
00:06:23,992 --> 00:06:26,379
and it will come out white,

233
00:06:26,399 --> 00:06:28,052
without any illness.

234
00:06:28,072 --> 00:06:28,986
Two proofs,

235
00:06:29,006 --> 00:06:30,289
from your Lord,

236
00:06:30,309 --> 00:06:31,463
to Pharaoh.

237
00:06:31,483 --> 00:06:32,720
Go to Pharaoh,

238
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:34,025
he was told.

239
00:06:34,045 --> 00:06:35,697
He has transgressed.

240
00:06:35,717 --> 00:06:37,874
Musa knew who Pharaoh was,

241
00:06:37,894 --> 00:06:39,485
and that they held

242
00:06:39,505 --> 00:06:41,894
a killing against him there.

243
00:06:41,914 --> 00:06:43,659
He did not refuse.

244
00:06:43,679 --> 00:06:45,524
He asked for help.

245
00:06:45,544 --> 00:06:46,320
My Lord,

246
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:48,359
expand my chest for me,

247
00:06:48,379 --> 00:06:50,769
and ease my task for me.

248
00:06:50,789 --> 00:06:53,314
Untie the knot from my tongue,

249
00:06:53,334 --> 00:06:55,155
so that they understand

250
00:06:55,175 --> 00:06:56,283
my speech.

251
00:06:56,303 --> 00:06:57,388
And give me

252
00:06:57,408 --> 00:06:59,473
a helper from my family:

253
00:06:59,493 --> 00:07:01,067
Harun, my brother.

254
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:02,186
Allah answered:

255
00:07:02,206 --> 00:07:03,383
you have been

256
00:07:03,403 --> 00:07:04,961
granted your request,

257
00:07:04,981 --> 00:07:05,952
O Musa.

258
00:07:05,972 --> 00:07:07,839
Then came an instruction

259
00:07:07,859 --> 00:07:09,235
worth remembering.

260
00:07:09,255 --> 00:07:10,782
Go, both of you,

261
00:07:10,802 --> 00:07:11,717
to Pharaoh,

262
00:07:11,737 --> 00:07:13,295
the man who said:

263
00:07:13,315 --> 00:07:15,989
I am your most exalted lord.

264
00:07:16,009 --> 00:07:18,626
Speak to him with gentle speech,

265
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:19,914
so that perhaps

266
00:07:19,934 --> 00:07:21,309
he will remember,

267
00:07:21,329 --> 00:07:22,246
or fear.

268
00:07:22,266 --> 00:07:23,272
Gentle words,

269
00:07:23,292 --> 00:07:25,113
for the greatest tyrant

270
00:07:25,133 --> 00:07:26,518
of his time.

271
00:07:26,538 --> 00:07:27,958
In Pharaoh's court,

272
00:07:27,978 --> 00:07:28,847
Musa said:

273
00:07:28,867 --> 00:07:30,227
send the Children

274
00:07:30,247 --> 00:07:31,992
of Israel with us.

275
00:07:32,012 --> 00:07:33,143
Pharaoh answered

276
00:07:33,163 --> 00:07:34,631
with a question.

277
00:07:34,651 --> 00:07:36,350
Who is your Lord?

278
00:07:36,370 --> 00:07:37,377
Musa replied:

279
00:07:37,397 --> 00:07:38,159
our Lord

280
00:07:38,179 --> 00:07:39,586
is He who gave

281
00:07:39,606 --> 00:07:41,119
everything its form,

282
00:07:41,139 --> 00:07:43,029
and then guided it.

283
00:07:43,049 --> 00:07:44,962
Pharaoh gathered the most

284
00:07:44,982 --> 00:07:46,941
skilled magicians in Egypt

285
00:07:46,961 --> 00:07:48,566
on a festival day,

286
00:07:48,586 --> 00:07:50,147
before the crowds.

287
00:07:50,167 --> 00:07:51,942
They threw their ropes

288
00:07:51,962 --> 00:07:52,876
and staffs,

289
00:07:52,896 --> 00:07:54,487
and by their magic

290
00:07:54,507 --> 00:07:55,822
the ropes seemed

291
00:07:55,842 --> 00:07:57,679
to move like snakes.

292
00:07:57,699 --> 00:08:00,280
Musa felt fear inside himself.

293
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:01,122
Fear not,

294
00:08:01,142 --> 00:08:02,197
Allah said.

295
00:08:02,217 --> 00:08:03,731
You are superior.

296
00:08:03,751 --> 00:08:04,606
Throw what

297
00:08:04,626 --> 00:08:06,739
is in your right hand.

298
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:08,502
Musa threw his staff,

299
00:08:08,522 --> 00:08:10,527
and it swallowed everything

300
00:08:10,547 --> 00:08:12,023
they had made.

301
00:08:12,043 --> 00:08:13,910
The magicians knew magic

302
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:16,179
better than anyone in Egypt,

303
00:08:16,199 --> 00:08:17,376
and they knew

304
00:08:17,396 --> 00:08:19,187
this was not magic.

305
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:21,688
They fell down in prostration.

306
00:08:21,708 --> 00:08:22,562
We believe

307
00:08:22,582 --> 00:08:25,532
in the Lord of Harun and Musa.

308
00:08:25,552 --> 00:08:27,465
Pharaoh threatened to cut

309
00:08:27,485 --> 00:08:28,753
off their hands

310
00:08:28,773 --> 00:08:31,071
and feet and crucify them.

311
00:08:31,091 --> 00:08:32,143
They answered:

312
00:08:32,163 --> 00:08:34,230
decide whatever you will.

313
00:08:34,250 --> 00:08:35,887
You can only decide

314
00:08:35,907 --> 00:08:38,028
about this worldly life.

315
00:08:38,048 --> 00:08:39,793
Still Pharaoh refused.

316
00:08:39,813 --> 00:08:42,062
Allah sent signs upon Egypt:

317
00:08:42,082 --> 00:08:44,037
the flood, locusts, lice,

318
00:08:44,057 --> 00:08:45,525
frogs and blood.

319
00:08:45,545 --> 00:08:46,414
Each time,

320
00:08:46,434 --> 00:08:47,748
they begged Musa

321
00:08:47,768 --> 00:08:49,926
to pray for it to end,

322
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:51,582
and promised to let

323
00:08:51,602 --> 00:08:52,979
his people go.

324
00:08:52,999 --> 00:08:54,650
Each time it ended,

325
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:56,699
they broke their word.

326
00:08:56,719 --> 00:08:58,462
Then Allah told Musa:

327
00:08:58,482 --> 00:08:59,750
travel by night

328
00:08:59,770 --> 00:09:01,285
with My servants.

329
00:09:01,305 --> 00:09:03,142
You will be pursued.

330
00:09:03,162 --> 00:09:04,476
Pharaoh sent men

331
00:09:04,496 --> 00:09:07,298
to every city to gather an army,

332
00:09:07,318 --> 00:09:09,853
and they followed at sunrise.

333
00:09:09,873 --> 00:09:10,589
The sea

334
00:09:10,609 --> 00:09:12,536
was in front of them,

335
00:09:12,556 --> 00:09:14,761
and the army was behind.

336
00:09:14,781 --> 00:09:16,616
Musa's people cried out:

337
00:09:16,636 --> 00:09:19,117
we are going to be caught.

338
00:09:19,137 --> 00:09:20,528
Musa said: No.

339
00:09:20,548 --> 00:09:22,523
My Lord is with me.

340
00:09:22,543 --> 00:09:24,342
He will guide me.

341
00:09:24,362 --> 00:09:25,322
Those words,

342
00:09:25,342 --> 00:09:26,381
from a man

343
00:09:26,401 --> 00:09:28,696
with the sea at his back,

344
00:09:28,716 --> 00:09:30,307
are among the best

345
00:09:30,327 --> 00:09:32,218
known in the Quran.

346
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:33,750
Allah inspired Musa:

347
00:09:33,770 --> 00:09:36,482
strike the sea with your staff.

348
00:09:36,502 --> 00:09:37,324
It split,

349
00:09:37,344 --> 00:09:38,981
and each side stood

350
00:09:39,001 --> 00:09:41,528
like a great towering mountain.

351
00:09:41,548 --> 00:09:43,093
A dry path opened

352
00:09:43,113 --> 00:09:44,580
through the middle,

353
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,362
and Musa

354
00:09:45,382 --> 00:09:47,663
and all who were with him

355
00:09:47,683 --> 00:09:48,976
walked across.

356
00:09:48,996 --> 00:09:50,679
Pharaoh and his army

357
00:09:50,699 --> 00:09:52,213
followed them in.

358
00:09:52,233 --> 00:09:54,899
Then the sea closed over them.

359
00:09:54,919 --> 00:09:55,681
Musa and

360
00:09:55,701 --> 00:09:57,858
those with him were saved,

361
00:09:57,878 --> 00:09:59,025
all together.

362
00:09:59,045 --> 00:10:01,165
The others were drowned.

363
00:10:01,185 --> 00:10:03,343
As the water overtook him,

364
00:10:03,363 --> 00:10:04,921
Pharaoh finally said:

365
00:10:04,941 --> 00:10:05,750
I believe

366
00:10:05,770 --> 00:10:07,729
there is no god except

367
00:10:07,749 --> 00:10:09,432
the One the Children

368
00:10:09,452 --> 00:10:11,334
of Israel believe in.

369
00:10:11,354 --> 00:10:13,251
The answer came: now?

370
00:10:13,271 --> 00:10:15,484
When before you disobeyed?

371
00:10:15,504 --> 00:10:17,003
So today We will

372
00:10:17,023 --> 00:10:18,306
save your body,

373
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:19,778
so that you may

374
00:10:19,798 --> 00:10:20,791
be a sign

375
00:10:20,811 --> 00:10:23,530
for those who come after you.

376
00:10:23,550 --> 00:10:24,695
Centuries later,

377
00:10:24,715 --> 00:10:26,274
the Prophet Muhammad,

378
00:10:26,294 --> 00:10:27,898
peace be upon him,

379
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:29,187
came to Madinah

380
00:10:29,207 --> 00:10:31,350
and found the Jews fasting

381
00:10:31,370 --> 00:10:33,437
on the day of Ashura.

382
00:10:33,457 --> 00:10:34,634
They told him

383
00:10:34,654 --> 00:10:36,521
it was the day Allah

384
00:10:36,541 --> 00:10:37,947
saved the Children

385
00:10:37,967 --> 00:10:40,171
of Israel from their enemy,

386
00:10:40,191 --> 00:10:42,035
so Musa fasted it.

387
00:10:42,055 --> 00:10:42,832
He said:

388
00:10:42,852 --> 00:10:44,443
we have more claim

389
00:10:44,463 --> 00:10:46,253
over Musa than you.

390
00:10:46,273 --> 00:10:47,786
So he fasted it,

391
00:10:47,806 --> 00:10:49,489
and told the Muslims

392
00:10:49,509 --> 00:10:50,748
to fast it.

393
00:10:50,768 --> 00:10:51,990
It is recorded

394
00:10:52,010 --> 00:10:53,477
in Sahih al-Bukhari,

395
00:10:53,497 --> 00:10:56,032
number two thousand and four.

396
00:10:56,052 --> 00:10:58,211
Look back at the story.

397
00:10:58,231 --> 00:11:00,252
A mother who let go.

398
00:11:00,272 --> 00:11:02,567
A man who made a mistake,

399
00:11:02,587 --> 00:11:04,040
and turned straight

400
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:05,437
back to Allah.

401
00:11:05,457 --> 00:11:07,139
A stranger who asked

402
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:08,536
only for good.

403
00:11:08,556 --> 00:11:09,364
A prophet

404
00:11:09,384 --> 00:11:11,726
with a knot in his tongue,

405
00:11:11,746 --> 00:11:13,336
who asked for help

406
00:11:13,356 --> 00:11:15,009
instead of refusing.

407
00:11:15,029 --> 00:11:16,404
And gentle words,

408
00:11:16,424 --> 00:11:18,039
even for Pharaoh.

409
00:11:18,059 --> 00:11:19,189
When the sea

410
00:11:19,209 --> 00:11:21,734
was ahead and the army behind,

411
00:11:21,754 --> 00:11:22,945
he said only:

412
00:11:22,965 --> 00:11:24,940
my Lord is with me.

413
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,561
That is the story of Musa.
